---
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy | ML4EA" description="How the ML4EA companion portal handles account, participation, and instructor-verification information.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Privacy" title="A limited record for responsible access." description="The portal collects the account, participation, and professional information needed to support the community and protect instructor resources." accent="cyan" />

  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="container privacy-layout">
      <aside>
        <p class="eyebrow">Effective</p>
        <p><time datetime="2026-07-22">July 22, 2026</time></p>
        <a class="text-link" href="mailto:yjin@usc.edu">Privacy questions</a>
      </aside>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Information collected</h2>
        <p>Email-code authentication stores your email address, account identifier, and session information through Supabase. If you participate in discussions, the portal stores your chosen display name, posts, replies, and any moderation reports you submit. An instructor application additionally collects institution, department, position, institutional-profile URL, optional course context, review status, and administrative decision information.</p>

        <h2>How information is used</h2>
        <p>Account information is used to authenticate you and attribute participation. Discussion information is used to operate and moderate the community. Instructor-application information is used only to evaluate eligibility for protected teaching resources, administer that access, prevent misuse, and communicate about the application when necessary.</p>

        <h2>Visibility and sharing</h2>
        <p>Public discussion posts, replies, and chosen display names can be read by anyone. Account email addresses are not displayed with discussion content. Teaching Practice discussions are limited to approved instructors and portal administrators. Moderation reports are available only to authorized administrators.</p>
        <p>Instructor applications are not public. Database policies restrict each application to its applicant and authorized portal administrators. Proposed book corrections and teaching resources submitted through the portal repository are generally public and are also subject to GitHub’s privacy practices. Portal information is not sold or used for advertising.</p>

        <h2>Protected materials</h2>
        <p>Instructor resources are kept in a private storage bucket. Approved accounts receive short-lived signed download links. Approval does not transfer copyright or permit redistribution.</p>

        <h2>Retention and requests</h2>
        <p>Account, discussion, moderation, application, and protected administrator records are retained while needed to operate the portal, administer access, preserve review history, and prevent misuse. To request correction or deletion of your portal account or related information, contact <a href="mailto:yjin@usc.edu">yjin@usc.edu</a>. Public GitHub submissions must be managed through the corresponding GitHub repository. Some limited records may be retained when necessary for security, legal obligations, or misuse prevention.</p>

        <h2>Security and changes</h2>
        <p>The portal uses verified email sign-in, Row Level Security, private storage, and expiring links. No internet service can guarantee absolute security. Material changes to this notice will be recorded on this page and may also be announced through portal updates.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
